    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d624">

                <pb facs="0746" n="686" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg686"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr.
                            Olney</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-08-20"><hi rendition="#italic">August 20,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 495.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: For transmission to your colleague, the
                    Secretary of the Navy, I have the honor to inclose herewith two copies of a Blue
                    Book “Report on the rule of the road at sea,” which was to-day issued from the
                    office of publication.</p>
                <p>It must be regretted that a postponement of this important subject has been
                    resolved by the select committee of the House of Commons, by which decision an
                    absence of all fixed understanding internationally is, unhappily, caused.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d624-a1.xml" xpointer="d624-a1"/>
